---
title: Low Fat Restaurant style Matar Paneer
description: Recipe for a low fat restaurant style matar paneer, made healthier, so it is no longer an indulgence, but transformed into a simple everyday curry. 
image: https://www.saffrontrail.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/01/low-fat-restaurant-style-matar-paneer-03.jpg
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
cuisine: Indian, north indian
time required: 40 minutes
source: https://www.saffrontrail.com/low-fat-restaurant-style-matar-paneer-recipe
servings: 4
yield: 4 people
---

Heat @oil{1%tsp} in a #pan{} and dry roast @cashewnuts{1%tbsp}(broken) until very lightly golden. Remove and allow to cool.

Add @ginger{1%tsp}(grated) and @garlic{6%cloves}(sliced) to the same pan along with @onion{2}(finely sliced). Cook on a low-medium flame with a pinch of @salt{} for ~{8-10%minutes} until the onions are soft.

Stir in @tomatoes{3}(coarsely chopped) with @turmeric powder{1/2%tsp}. Allow to cook for ~{7-8%minutes} until the tomatoes collapse and turn into a mush.

Transfer the contents of the pan into a small mixer/blender. Combine @turmeric powder{1/2%tsp}, @red chilli powder{1%tsp}, @coriander powder{2%tsp}, and @cumin powder{1%tsp} and blend to a fine puree using up to @water{1/2%cup} to aid the blending process.

Pour this puree into the same pan. Season with @salt{} and simmer for ~{3-4%minutes}.

Add @green peas{1%cup}(frozen or fresh boiled) to this gravy along with @paneer{200%g}(cut into 1 cm cubes) and simmer for ~{5%minutes} so that the spices infuse into the peas and paneer.

Sprinkle @garam masala powder{1/2%tsp} and @kasuri methi{1%tsp}(dried fenugreek leaves). Give it one last stir and remove into a serving bowl.